AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015> "Lattice angle is a quality of a unit cell which describes the angle between three axes in a unit cell."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> (primitive unit cell)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> "primitive unit cell"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> "primitive unit cell is a unit cell that contains only single lattice point and has the smallest possible unit cell volume."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> <http://org.semanticweb.owlapi/error#Error2>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> <http://org.semanticweb.owlapi/error#Error3>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000017> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000018> (conventional unit cell)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000018> "conventional unit cell"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000018> "conventional unit cell is a unit cell with the full symmetry of the crystal lattice, i.e., it may contain more that one lattice point."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000018> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> (direction Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "direction Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "Direction Miller indices define the components of a sinlge vector in the given direction in a crystal's conventional unit cell. Usually, direction Miller indices are reduced to the lowest set of integers. Direction Miller indices must be written in square brackets, e.g., [hkl]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "[111]")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> (family of directions Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "family of directions Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "<111>")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "Set of directions Miller indices define the components of symmetrically equivalent directions in a crystal lattice. Set of directions Miller indices must be written as <hkl>."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> (plane Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "plane Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "Plane Miller indices define the reciprocals of the fractional intercepts the plane makes with the crystallographic axes, reduced to the lowest set of integers. 
For example, if a plane crosses [100] axis at 1/h, [010 ] axis at 1/k, and [001] axis at 1/l, then such plane is denoted as (hkl) plane. If a plane is parallel to one of the axes, then the corresponding Miller index is 0.
Plane Miller indices must be written in round brackets, e.g., (hkl)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "(hkl)")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> (family of planes Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "family of planes Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "Set of planes Miller indices define set of symmetrically equivalent planes. Set of planes must be written in curly brackets, e.g., {hkl}."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "{111}")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> (point coordinate datum)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "Current decision is not to import 'cartesian spatial coordinate datum' (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000400) cause it denotes spatial regions, and we model lattice points and atoms in voids as sites."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "point coordinate datum"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "Point coordinate datum define the coordinates of a point within a conventional unit cell of a crystal. Point Miller indices must be given in round brackets separated by commas, e.g., (x, y, z)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "(1,1,1)")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> (atomic plane)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> "atomic plane"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> "Atomic plane is a 2D fiat object part which has atoms as it parts and is located in some crystallogphic plane, i.e., the positions of atoms relative to each other are defined via the characterisitics of the crystallogphic plane."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33250>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000025> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> (crystal system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "crystal system"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "Crystal system is a quality of a (real) crystal which defines its symmetry based on the rotational and mirror symmetries of the actual atomic arrangements."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> (lattice centering)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> "lattice centering"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> "Lattice centering is an intensive quality ofa crystal lattice which the geometric arrangement of lattice points in a unit cell. It is specified by one of the 4 lattice centering value."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>) ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036>)))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> (crystal system value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> "crystal system value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> "crystal system value is a categorical value specification which describes the grouping of
crystal system  based on the rotational and mirror symmetries of their actual atomic arrangements in the  crystal. The specific values are triclinic, monoclinic, orthorhombic, tetragonal, trigonal, hexagonal, and cubic."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000391>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> (lattice centering value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> "lattice centering value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> "Lattice centering value is a categorical value specification which describes th geometric arrangement of lattice points in a unit cell with one of the values: primitive, body centered, face centered, base centered."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000037> (alpha angle)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000037> "alpha angle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000037> "α anlge"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000037> "α anlge is an angle in a unit cell between y- and z-axes."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000037> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000038> (beta angle)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000038> "beta angle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000038> "β anlge"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000038> "β anlge is an angle in a unit cell between x- and z-axes."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000038> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000039> (gamma angle)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000039> "gamma angle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000039> "γ angle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000039> "γ anlge is an angle in a unit cell between x- and y-axes.")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000039> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000015>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> (crystallographic entity in cubic system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> "'immaterial entity' and ('part of' some 
('crystal lattice' and ('has quality' some 
('crystal system' and ('specified by value' value cubic)))))")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> "crystallographic entity in cubic system"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> ObjectUnionOf(ObjectIntersectionOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> ObjectHasValue(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035>)))))) ObjectIntersectionOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> ObjectHasValue(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035>))))))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> ObjectHasSelf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000042> (grain orientation)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000042> "grain orientation"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000042> "Grain orientation is an intensive quality of grains in material's microstructure, which describes the crystallographic orientation in respect to the external (sample's) reference frame. Grain orientation can be a quality of an individual grain / crystallite or of a polycrystal, i.e., several grsins with similar crystallographic orientations.
Grain orientation can be specified by either texture fibers or texture components. When several grains exhibit similar orientations, then the material exhibits a specific crystallographic texture."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000042> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000042> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000663>))

